      "description": "Generic late-1980s front-drive economy sedan engine authored from first-principles specifications rather than a specific production unit: 79 x 81.5 mm (1,598 cc) inline four, 9.2:1 compression, belt-driven single overhead cam with two valves per cylinder, two-barrel carburetor on a long-runner manifold, distributor mechanical advance, 1-3-4-2 firing, cast four-into-one manifold with unequal primaries, and a single pipe with a stock muffler. Converted one-to-one from the engine-sim script assets/engines/sedan16_sohc_i4.mr (same geometry, gas path, cams, timing, fuel, vehicle, per-cylinder sound attenuation, mild_exhaust IR and hf_gain/jitter/noise conditioning). Port flow, cam, friction, and presentation values are authoring estimates for audition, not measurements."
